This product uses public amateur-radio reference data supplied by its configured
sources. Those datasets remain subject to their respective providers' terms.

The OM0RX-xLog icon was created specifically for this project.

Bundled contest country prefixes are from Jim Reisert AD1C's Contest Country
Files #3533 (12 October 2025). cty.csv is the published file with LF line
endings. The original permission notice is in
Sources/XLogCore/Resources/CTY-COPYRIGHT.txt.
Source: https://www.country-files.com/cty/download/3533/cty-3533.zip

The dated country reference pack uses country tables developed by Martin OK1RR,
distributed by CQRLOG at revision 4adb0e70bf29faefc3b203bc355796cd0c6201fe.
The data is separately credited and is not covered by the upstream parser's
GPL v2 licence. The source table hashes and normalization details are in the
pack itself. See https://github.com/ok2cqr/cqrlog-cnty-files/blob/4adb0e70bf29faefc3b203bc355796cd0c6201fe/data/README.md

DXCC map geometry: amazingproducer/dxcc-world-map, pinned in
Sources/XLogCore/Resources/DXCC_BOUNDARIES_SOURCE.md. Ham Mission Control is
adapted from Billy NZ3C's MIT-licensed project; its notices, asset origins and
hashes are under prototype/vendor/ham-mission-control and
prototype/public/hm-control-assets. Individual assets and reference data are
subject to their credited providers' terms.

The desktop application includes code adapted from
OM0RX-xCluster by Oliver Bross OM0RX, GPL-3.0-only, source revision
776b7b04ffa5a9057f1e909339393549a103836b.

The Mac direct-station integration is based on OM0RX-xCat XCatCore by
Oliver Bross OM0RX, GPL-3.0-only. Original source revision:
b8f2e95527425247623dae366f94114bc0e1e94e, with integration-time source
diff SHA-256 01439189a7d6aac7356c5cb36a1b8c9c9015a4185d3ab1837f9d917d750d824d.

The read-only chaser and DX calendar are independently implemented from the
ShackCQ GPL-3.0-only behavioral contracts at revision
f5bdbd9186f33d3a257971a08a222ae622a9c66e. Public spot publishers and 425DXN retain
their own data terms and visible source attribution. No third-party calendar
code or raw provider data is bundled.

The initial CQ WW CW, CQ WPX CW, CQ WW SSB, CQ WPX SSB, Oceania DX CW,
Oceania DX SSB, SAC CW, SAC SSB, the isolated NAQP CW/SSB/RTTY preview,
and the inactive ARRL RTTY Roundup station-policy preview
in Sources/XContestCore/PilotRules.swift, Sources/XContestCore/OceaniaRules.swift,
Sources/XContestCore/SACRules.swift, Sources/XContestCore/Cabrillo.swift,
Sources/XContestCore/NAQPRules.swift, and Sources/XContestCore/ARRLRTTYRoundupRule.swift
is a Swift translation adapted from
Not1MM by Michael Bridak (GPL-3.0-or-later), using Oliver Bross's read-only
contest-sw fork at revision 7c8b499225a73f7f8f792246881bd7aefc05452f. The ARRL
comparison additionally uses `not1mm/plugins/arrl_rtty_ru.py`; operational rule
authority remains the independently pinned ARRL primary documents.
The translated source paths are not1mm/plugins/cq_ww_cw.py,
not1mm/plugins/cq_wpx_cw.py, not1mm/plugins/cq_ww_ssb.py,
not1mm/plugins/cq_wpx_ssb.py, not1mm/plugins/oceania_dx_cw.py,
not1mm/plugins/oceania_dx_ssb.py, not1mm/plugins/sac_cw.py,
not1mm/plugins/sac_ssb.py, not1mm/lib/ham_utility.py,
not1mm/plugins/naqp_cw.py, not1mm/plugins/naqp_ssb.py,
not1mm/plugins/naqp_rtty.py, not1mm/plugins/arrl_rtty_ru.py,
not1mm/lib/database.py and duplicate dispatch in not1mm/__main__.py. The
translation was modified for OM0RX-xLog on 17-18 October 2026.
The NAQP export layout also references the NCJ Cabrillo template at
https://ncjweb.com/NAQP_Cabrillo_Template.txt and the ADIF 3.1.8 annotated
specification at https://www.adif.org/318/ADIF_318_annotated.htm, both retrieved
18 October 2026.

